  "notes": "Airport authority treated as governmental (GAAP) because it presents a governmental fund balance sheet and statement of revenues, expenditures and changes in fund balance (p3-4); no business-type funds. Receipts/disbursements are from the governmental fund statement (p4), accrual basis; the budgetary comparison schedule on p5 is on a budgetary (cash-like) basis and differs (resources 478,174 vs revenues 566,124; reconciled on p6). Detail is the budget schedule only (the fund statement has no more detailed schedule); it is a different basis from the receipts/disbursements lists. Balance sheet uses the government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1), single unlabeled column; balances: 10,595,702 = 91,353 + 10,504,349. Statement of Activities p2: net position 10,770,165 to 10,504,349. Expenditures are listed by object, so they were placed under general government with review (airport has no function category). (Correction: budget schedule 'Loan collections' 4,177 is principal collected on the note receivable, so it is recorded as detail section other financing; the printed Total resources 478,174 includes it.) Read pages 1-6 of 6"
